From 69f37d512250ebe27e0922a69819121f3fd1d692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:21:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] plugin,daemon: damp the sandbox-churn feedback loop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Kubelet retries failed sandbox creation every few seconds with no
meaningful backoff, so any meshnet ADD failure mode that a retry cannot fix
becomes a permanent ~3s create/teardown loop that also drags every peer of
the pod through interface flaps and skip-list rewrites. Reduce both the
loop's fuel and its noise:

- Park, do not fail, on peer instability: when EnsureVethWire reports the
  PEER pod's netns vanished (koko.NamespaceGoneError for the peer's
  namespace), set the existing Skip flag and continue — identical to the
  established peer-not-alive contract; the peer completes the wire on its
  own next ADD. A vanished LOCAL netns still fails the ADD (our sandbox is
  genuinely bad).
- Collect genuine same-node wiring failures per link (errors.Join) instead
  of aborting at the first one: one bad link no longer hides the state of
  the other nine, and the combined error names every failed link.
- cmdDel refuses to remove protected interface names (eth0/lo/empty) as
  defense in depth; the delegated interface is untouchable in every path.
- SkipReverse's own-list filter dropped every entry sharing EITHER the
  peer name OR the link id (De Morgan bug); entries are now removed only
  on an exact (peer, linkId) match via keepSkippedEntry.
- DeletePodWires logged '[WIRE-DELETE]:All grpc-wires ... deleted' at Info
  on every CNI DEL even with zero wires — reading as gRPC overlay churn in
  same-node/VXLAN labs during sandbox retry loops. The no-op case now logs
  at Debug; the real case reports the count.

Upstreamable.
